                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ff4243b-197b-3442-880c-1f87c32fb84c",
                        "entry_id": "22325e38-bcdd-3ac5-92af-81f8af570cfb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A warrant issued for someone to be taken into custody."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a33f0f1f-af89-4a6d-b479-08ad2d2e5c27",
                                "sense_id": "3ff4243b-197b-3442-880c-1f87c32fb84c",
                                "text": "Away George, away, raise the watch at Ludgate, and bring a Mittimus from the Iustice for this desperate villaine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14292fb0-d243-4834-9fc3-9fcced8b40a0",
                                "sense_id": "3ff4243b-197b-3442-880c-1f87c32fb84c",
                                "text": "But she pertinaciously refused to make any response. So that he was about to make her mittimus to Bridewell when I departed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48448fd2-8803-38e5-993c-211e51f112c8",
                        "entry_id": "22325e38-bcdd-3ac5-92af-81f8af570cfb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A writ for moving records from one court to another."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c9a12f0-e491-4f69-8c18-15150d09f8d9",
                                "sense_id": "48448fd2-8803-38e5-993c-211e51f112c8",
                                "text": "Next, sometimes the same clerk, but often a second clerk, who may not have been in the courtroom, types up the mittimus, the formal court order that directs corrections offers^([sic]) to commit someone to prison, and something could get lost in translation there."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
